From 8fdcb4bfa084887e135028b9568846c5c6ac1d10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/40] host_sim, HOST.md: guards from real data + per-user
 barrier before step; contract wording for dedup, ack, executor order,
 failures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

host_sim.py computed every guard as True and drained the outbox inline, so the
interaction 'guards are computed before call actions of the previous step are
executed' (HOST §1.3 + §2) was never exercised and engine mutants that drop a
guard survived. Now: separate outbox executor thread (50 ms polling), cart and
address data updated by idempotent local calls, cart_not_empty from the cart,
in_delivery_zone from the message text, users that hit the false branches
(empty cart on checkout, address outside the zone), expected final state per
user as the oracle, lost-update replay with the recorded guard values.
Regression: host_sim.py --no-barrier (literal old §1.3) -> exit 1 (0/30 users
as expected); default (barrier) -> exit 0.

HOST.md: §1.3 read-your-writes for guards (barrier or same-transaction calls,
guards may read the event); §1.2 dedup table with 24 h window instead of a set
inside the snapshot row; §1.5 cumulative getUpdates ack; §2 per-user FIFO
across responses, event data stored with actions, failure queue, timer due
time from commit, send is at-least-once; §5 deterministic engine errors and
document load time vs client timeout; §7 updated.

Integration note: the hunk for audit/host-perf/host_sim_mutants.py (host-perf audit
harness, not part of audit/integration) is dropped; HOST.md merges with 998a539 (engine-timers)
without textual conflicts, rules of both kept (reviewed by hand).

(cherry picked from commit c8bb903666211b690eb78e62d0791722eab0a8d9)

